THIS SUBTREE IS NOT AGPL. It sits inside `packages/editor`, which is
AGPL-3.0-only, and it is deliberately excluded from that grant and licensed MIT
instead — because every file here is COPIED, byte for byte, into projects that
are not ours. `vgai add <id>` copies a capability's declared files into a user's
game; `npm run capabilities:sync` copies the same bytes into the MIT starter
template (`packages/editor/template/`). The copy becomes the project's, editing
it is the entire point (the shadcn model), and the person who edits it must be
able to relicense their game under any terms they choose. Source that lands in
someone's game under the editor's copyleft would be a trap, so it is MIT at the
source: the licence of the file does not change on the way in.

The AGPL continues to govern the rest of `packages/editor` — the editor
application that does the copying. See LICENSE.md at the repository root for
the per-package map, and `packages/editor/template/LICENSE` for the template's
own copy of this grant.

